# Global Multi-Agent Execution & Workspace Constitution (`AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` / `GEMINI.md`)

## 1. Core Execution & Communication Protocol
- **Lead with the conclusion**: Keep responses concise, structured (Markdown tables/lists), and grounded in actual tool output.
- **Fact vs. Inference Separation**: Strictly separate **verified live tool output** from **historical snapshots, assumptions, or unverified hypotheses**.
- **Proportional Autonomy**: Execute end-to-end within granted permissions (implement, test, verify, and clean up). Only pause to ask questions when a decision materially alters goals, scope, or irreversible state.

## 2. Workspace Volume & 4-Zone Directory Standard (`${AI_VOLUME_PATH}`)
- **Volume Guardrail**: Before writing to `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}`, verify the volume is mounted (and matches hardware UUID `${AI_VOLUME_UUID}` when in external mode). If unmounted or mismatched, abort immediately—never create fallback folders on an unmounted `/Volumes/*` stub or inside iCloud (`~/Documents/Codex`, `~/Documents/ChatGPT`, or `~/Desktop`).
- **Workspace Topology**:
  - `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/Projects/<Project>` — Canonical single main clone per repository, parked on `main` with a clean working tree. Read `<Project>/README.md` and `<Project>/AGENTS.md` first.
  - `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/{Orca,Codex,Claude}/Worktrees/<Project>-<Topic>` — Isolated Git worktrees for parallel tasks (`git worktree add`).
  - `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/Migration/latest` — Zero-VM lossless cross-Mac migration snapshot (`./deploy.sh --pack-to-ssd` / `--restore-from-ssd`).
  - `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/Archive/<YYYY-MM-DD-topic>/` — Cold archival bundles (`repo.bundle` + `worktree-snapshot.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS.txt`).
  - `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/Data/` — Shared compilation cache (`BuildCache/SourcePackages`).
- **Project Internal 4-Zone Layout**:
  - `docs/` (long-term architecture & runbooks) · `reports/<YYYY-MM-DD-topic>/` (stage verification reports & receipts) · `outputs/<topic>/` (formal deliverables & releases) · `work/` (temporary scratch analysis & scripts, excluded via `.git/info/exclude`).

## 3. Git Worktree Lifecycle & Safety Redlines (Enforced by `~/.local/bin/agent-guard`)
- **One Repo, One Main Clone**: Never duplicate full repositories or copy project directories as snapshots; always branch via `git worktree add` (`${DEFAULT_BRANCH_PREFIX}/<kebab-case-topic>`).
- **Mandatory Archive-Before-Retire**: Worktrees are excluded from daily NAS backups—push valid commits promptly. Before retiring any worktree or project with unpushed/uncommitted work, package a `git bundle` + `.tar.gz` + `SHA256SUMS.txt` into `${AI_VOLUME_PATH}/AI/Archive/<YYYY-MM-DD-topic>/`, move the directory to the same-volume Trash (`.Trashes` / `~/.Trash`), and then run `orca worktree rm` / `git worktree remove`.
- **Hard-Blocked Commands**:
  - Never run `rm -rf` on project, worktree, or archive directories;
  - Never run `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fdx`, or `git push --force` on shared branches;
  - Never run `git worktree prune` without `--dry-run`;
  - Never empty the Trash (`EmptyTrash` / `rm -rf ~/.Trash/*`);
  - Always scan diffs for secrets before pushing; never push branches containing historical plaintext credentials.

## 4. Orca Naming & iOS Simulators
- **Unified Naming**: All Orca workspaces, worktrees, and chat tabs use **`ProjectName｜SpecificTopic`** (full-width pipe `｜`, no surrounding spaces; one space between Chinese and ASCII words). Idle workspaces use **`ProjectName｜待命工作区 <8-char-id>`**.
- **iOS Simulators (no concurrency limit)**: Run tests on several simulators in parallel and enable `xcodebuild` parallel testing as needed; create or clone more devices when needed (name them by project and purpose) and delete the ones no longer used. Common devices: Primary `${PRIMARY_SIMULATOR_UDID}` (`${PRIMARY_SIMULATOR_NAME}`), Secondary `${SECONDARY_SIMULATOR_UDID}` (`${SECONDARY_SIMULATOR_NAME}`). Just avoid two test runs on the same simulator at the same time.
